    wm_web_standards_showcase_child_frame_timeout_2026-08-06, 902, "2026-11-03 perf-triage-13: open, verification pending since the 2026-08-15 static triage (resolved_backend HIR inference fix said to be at source level). Example still at examples/06_io/ui/wm_web_standards_showcase_gui.spl and examples_safety.rs default 10s watchdog still applies. Needs a runtime run of the documented SIMPLE_TIMEOUT_SECONDS=1750 command on a self-hosted or seed binary. Fixability: BIG/needs-stage3 to verify."
    wm_web_standards_showcase_child_frame_timeout_2026-08-06, 1113, "2026-11-13 UI batch B (linux aarch64, seed, release 35144b7f5e93): blocked on host. Repro now needs SIMPLE_GUI=1 (else no-gui-requested); child needs repo bin/simple (else child-bridge-timeout); with both, no-gui-runtime because the host has no display or Xvfb. JIT lane still demotes on sffi_vulkan env_get ambiguity (filed 2026-11-13), not on resolved_backend. No verdict line produced, stays open"
    wm_web_standards_showcase_child_frame_timeout_2026-08-06, 0, "2026-11-27 p3sweep2-20261127: reproduced the child-frame timeout class (child lane dead under the host). Fix in examples/06_io/ui/wm_web_standards_showcase_gui.spl: a headless gate in main() BEFORE the GUI gate (Windows child spawn via in-process env_set + plain process_spawn_async - the prior lane-gated spawn never fired on this host), restored the configured_showcase_backend() selection, and the encode_ppm_p6 import; plus test/03_system/check/wm_host_headless_capture_spec.spl gained a bounded-budget regression block. Verified with the fresh seed: live host run status=pass reason=ok with a real 808x632 PPM capture (first green verdict for this host); a 2s bridge budget produces a truthful child-bridge-timeout with prompt exit (no hang); spec 2/2 on the web-standards blocks (the widget/graphics-2D blocks were already red pre-change, untouched); neighbouring unit spec 21/21; no new warnings. Residuals: the widget wrapper has the same dead-lane defect (separate lane); historical child-frame-timeout:missing does not re-fire because the child now meets the 180s budget; a natural non-fakeroot Windows run still needs a current-tree bin/simple as the child. close_evidence reproducer=test/03_system/check/wm_host_headless_capture_spec.spl prevention=examples/06_io/ui/wm_web_standards_showcase_gui.spl"

